        <h2>Summary / Description</h2>
        <div class="description">
          OBJECTIVES:<br>
During bed rest studies, the Case Report Form (CRF) provided a mechanism by which nursing and dietary staff, and other subject monitors, could record subject monitoring data. The information was then shared with each of the experiment teams as necessary. 
<div>
APPROACH:<br>
The CRF was comprised of the following forms:
</div><div></div><li>Medical Status and Vitals: a daily record of the subject's vital signs, including blood pressure, respiration rate, pulse, body temperature, and weight. The temperature and ambient humidity of the subject's room were also recorded daily. Height was measured once at the beginning of the pre-test, in-test, and post-test periods. 
</li><li>Daily Meal Status: a daily record of the times that breakfast, lunch, and dinner meals were started and completed. Any deviation from the dietary protocol was noted. 
</li><li>Stretching Session I and II: a daily record indicating whether two separate stretching sessions were completed during the 24-hour period. 
</li><li>Medication Log: a record of all medication given during the campaign, including the dosage, time of administration, medical indication, and outcome. 
</li><li>Protocol Deviation Summary: a record of any protocol deviations that might have occurred during the campaign. 
</li><li>Symptom Complaint Log: a record of all complaints reported by the subject during the campaign, the measures taken address the issue, and the resolution of the complaint. 
</li><li>Urine Collection Log: a record of all urine specimens collected during the campaign, including the weight and specific gravity of each specimen. 
</li><li>Water Intake Log: a daily record of water intake by the subject. 
</li><li>Fecal Collection Log: a record of the date, time, and weight of each bowel movement. 
</li><li>Emesis Log: a record of each emesis episode (if any), for the Artificial Gravity Pilot Study, including the measured weight of the emesis. 
</li><li>Test Specific CRF: each bed rest test had a test-specific CRF form to record details about each testing session. 
</li><li>Sample Collection CRF: specific details regarding the collection of each blood and saliva specimen was documented. 
<div>
These are the case report forms that were collected and documented during Campaign 11 and Campaign 19.</div></li><li>
Medical Status and Vitals: a daily record of the subject's vital signs, including blood pressure, respiration rate, pulse, body temperature, and weight. The temperature and ambient humidity of the subject's room were also recorded daily. Height is measured once at the beginning of the pre-test, in-test, and post-test periods. 
</li><li> Daily Meal Status: a daily record of the times that breakfast, lunch, and dinner meals were started and completed. Any deviation from the dietary protocol was noted. 
</li><li>Medication Log: a record of all medication given during the campaign, including the dosage, time of administration, medical indication, and outcome. 
</li><li> Issues Notice: a record of any issues, or protocol deviations that might have occurred during the campaign.  
</li><li> Symptom Complaint Log: a record of all complaints reported by the subject during the campaign, the measures taken address the issue, and the resolution of the complaint. 
</li><li> Water Intake and Output Log: a daily record of water and urine intake and output by the subject.
</li><li> Weight Chart: Subject weight is recorded pre, in and post-test in kilograms by bed rest day.   

<div>RESULTS:<br>
All experiments using the CRF have been completed. Tabular results are available for the public.</div></li>
